# fixedbugs, defect 556, lane b18-ffi, 2026-10-10 (panel 202's C2; the
# ffi-pragmatist's `tent`).
#
# A header holds `int counter;`, a tentative definition, which its `static
# inline bump` reads, and two modules bind `bump`, so each unit defines
# `counter`. Until 2026-10-10 the verdict was the platform's: on this Mac
# the two merged and the program printed `1` and `2`, and on Linux the link
# refused it, a multiple definition, at exit 2. Told at exit 1 on every
# platform, before anything links, on the group's string, since no group
# binds `counter`.
use fixedbugs556/counts

extern "fixedbugs-556-tentative.h"  #~ ffi_defined_twice
    function bump() -> i32

function main()
    print(bump())
    print(counts.counted())
